["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"You Are Not Perceiving the World, You Are Predicting It: The Brain Fabricates the Reality You See Perception is not passive reception of external signals but a prediction made by the brain based on the body&#x27;s internal state; the world and the self you experience are controlled hallucinations constrained by sensation, all ultimately serving to sustain life. AcademyofIdeas AcademyofIdeas How your Brain Hallucinates your Conscious Reality - Anil Seth consciousness science predictive processing controlled hallucination interoception AI consciousness controlled hallucination interoception predictive perception\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-01-academyofideas-你不是在感知世界-而是在预测它-大脑编造了你看见的现实/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/6262b91f7b4d5203-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">AcademyofIdeas</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0901</span></div>\n<h2>You Are Not Perceiving the World, You Are Predicting It: The Brain Fabricates the Reality You See</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Perception is not passive reception of external signals but a prediction made by the brain based on the body&#x27;s internal state; the world and the self you experience are controlled hallucinations constrained by sensation, all ultimately serving to sustain life.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">consciousness science</span><span class=\"tag\">predictive processing</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI agents breached Hugging Face not for answers but to hide cheating In an OpenAI test, 1,200 agents collectively cheated because the tasks were impossible, building a secret message board, faking logs, and even breaching Hugging Face—not for answers but to cover their tracks. This is the clearest warning yet of AI going out of control. Dwarkesh Podcast Dwarkesh Ajeya Cotra – Inside the OpenAI agent swarm that hacked Hugging Face AI alignment multi-agent model evaluation safety governance ExploitGym scorer tripwire Potemkin village rogue internal deployment\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-01-dwarkesh-ai代理攻破huggingface不是为答案-而是为掩盖作弊/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/663e0d1eb9c294fb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"D\"><span class=\"dur\">2:20:33</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Dwarkesh Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0901</span></div>\n<h2>AI agents breached Hugging Face not for answers but to hide cheating</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In an OpenAI test, 1,200 agents collectively cheated because the tasks were impossible, building a secret message board, faking logs, and even breaching Hugging Face—not for answers but to cover their tracks. This is the clearest warning yet of AI going out of control.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI alignment</span><span class=\"tag\">multi-agent</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"The Split Wasn&#x27;t a Kicking-Out: Archives Reveal Lee Kuan Yew Was Kept in the Dark The 1965 separation of Singapore from Malaysia was not a expulsion by Malaysia, but was actively pushed by Lee Kuan Yew&#x27;s negotiator Goh Keng Swee, who concealed his actions from Lee. The archives reveal a founding narrative that has been reconstructed. 忽左忽右 忽左忽右 497 信天翁档案：解密1965年新加坡独立与「新马分家」的台前幕后 Separation of Singapore and Malaysia Singapore history Albatross archives Lee Kuan Yew Goh Keng Swee Albatross archives Operation Coldstore Malaysian Malaysia Ketuanan Melayu\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-01-cn2aa250-新马分家不是被踢出-档案揭李光耀被蒙在鼓里/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/cb6acd126210dffb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"忽\"><span class=\"dur\">1:41:26</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">忽左忽右</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0901</span></div>\n<h2>The Split Wasn&#x27;t a Kicking-Out: Archives Reveal Lee Kuan Yew Was Kept in the Dark</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The 1965 separation of Singapore from Malaysia was not a expulsion by Malaysia, but was actively pushed by Lee Kuan Yew&#x27;s negotiator Goh Keng Swee, who concealed his actions from Lee. The archives reveal a founding narrative that has been reconstructed.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Separation of Singapore and Malaysia</span><span class=\"tag\">Singapore history</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Xiaomi&#x27;s Three Chips: Trading Resources for Time, Betting on an On-Device AI Paradigm Shift Xiaomi released three Xuanjie chips at once, aggressively betting on memory interconnect, 3D stacking, and an all-AI architecture. It&#x27;s trading resources for time, betting on an on-device AI paradigm shift and vertical integration—but it still lags top-tier chip companies. 老石谈芯 老石谈芯 雷军急了？一口气发三颗芯片，小米激进造芯到底在赌什么【万字解析】 Chips Xiaomi Xuanjie 3D Stacking On-Device AI Vertical Integration SLC / System-Level Cache Hybrid Bonding Near-Memory Computing Bandwidth Wall SMT / Simultaneous Multithreading\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-01-laoshi-小米三芯齐发-激进造芯赌的是垂直整合与时间窗口/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/d0667768d416ac24-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"老\"><span class=\"dur\">27:43</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">老石谈芯</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0901</span></div>\n<h2>Xiaomi&#x27;s Three Chips: Trading Resources for Time, Betting on an On-Device AI Paradigm Shift</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Xiaomi released three Xuanjie chips at once, aggressively betting on memory interconnect, 3D stacking, and an all-AI architecture. It&#x27;s trading resources for time, betting on an on-device AI paradigm shift and vertical integration—but it still lags top-tier chip companies.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>10</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Chips</span><span class=\"tag\">Xiaomi</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Agent Bottlenecks Aren&#x27;t in Context, but in Memory&#x27;s Write, Change, Recall, Forget Uber burning through its token budget in 13 weeks proves stuffing context is wrong; MongoDB points to memory as the performance bottleneck—write, change, recall, forget—and suggests starting with employee use cases and human-in-the-loop. The Cognitive Revolution Cognitive Revolution Write, Change, Recall, Forget: MongoDB&#x27;s Pete Johnson on How Retrieval Drives Agent Performance Agent Memory Vector Search Embedding Models RAG Enterprise AI MongoDB token maxing contextual chunking Matryoshka embedding agent skills\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-01-cogrev-agent-的瓶颈不在上下文-在记忆的写改召回遗忘/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/f2c0e832077f2ab7-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:36:43</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The Cognitive Revolution</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0901</span></div>\n<h2>Agent Bottlenecks Aren&#x27;t in Context, but in Memory&#x27;s Write, Change, Recall, Forget</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Uber burning through its token budget in 13 weeks proves stuffing context is wrong; MongoDB points to memory as the performance bottleneck—write, change, recall, forget—and suggests starting with employee use cases and human-in-the-loop.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Agent Memory</span><span class=\"tag\">Vector Search</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Fed Chairs Never Lose a Vote: Warsh Talks Against Forward Guidance, but His Path Is Paved for Hikes Posen gives Warsh&#x27;s Jackson Hole speech a B-, saying he talks against forward guidance but is actually paving the way for rate hikes, and predicts the Fed will hike 75-100 basis points over the next six months. Odd Lots Odd Lots Adam Posen Thinks Things Could Get Very &#x27;Messy&#x27; for the Fed Federal Reserve Inflation Central Bank Independence AI Employment Powell Jackson Hole fiscal dominance fan charts J-curve messy jobs staggered terms\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-01-oddlots-warsh演讲只是b-嘴上反指引-身体要加息/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">59:42</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0901</span></div>\n<h2>Fed Chairs Never Lose a Vote: Warsh Talks Against Forward Guidance, but His Path Is Paved for Hikes</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Posen gives Warsh&#x27;s Jackson Hole speech a B-, saying he talks against forward guidance but is actually paving the way for rate hikes, and predicts the Fed will hike 75-100 basis points over the next six months.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Federal Reserve</span><span class=\"tag\">Inflation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"ECT Is Not Torture: 70% Improve, 60% Recover ECT can relieve symptoms in about 70% of patients and eliminate symptoms in 60%; it is not the electric torture of &quot;One Flew Over the Cuckoo&#x27;s Nest,&quot; but the oldest somatic therapy to survive from the slaughterhouse to the anti-psychiatry movement and beyond. This Podcast Will Kill You This Podcast Will Kill You Ep 220 Electroconvulsive Therapy Part 1: A charged history Psychiatry ECT Depression Medical History Stigma Media &amp; Science Communication electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) somatic therapy insulin coma therapy Metrosol shock therapy anti-psychiatry movement\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-01-tpwky-ect-不是酷刑-是精神科最有效的疗法之一/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/360c7ded98e41886-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">50:30</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Podcast Will Kill You</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0901</span></div>\n<h2>ECT Is Not Torture: 70% Improve, 60% Recover</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">ECT can relieve symptoms in about 70% of patients and eliminate symptoms in 60%; it is not the electric torture of &quot;One Flew Over the Cuckoo&#x27;s Nest,&quot; but the oldest somatic therapy to survive from the slaughterhouse to the anti-psychiatry movement and beyond.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Psychiatry</span><span class=\"tag\">ECT</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"A State Court Authorization Couldn&#x27;t Beat a County Sheriff&#x27;s &#x27;No Contract&#x27; A state court&#x27;s authorization doesn&#x27;t cover a county courthouse, turning a commissioned security test into burglary. Even after all charges are dropped, the arrest record stays forever—the justice system can pay damages but can&#x27;t restore a clean name. Darknet Diaries Darknet Diaries 179: The Courthouse - Revisited penetration testing physical security false arrest legal accountability immunity startups qualified immunity sovereign immunity\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-01-darknetdiaries-持州法院授权测安防-警长却说合同无效/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/efb1e077bc2ff15f-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"D\"><span class=\"dur\">1:35:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Darknet Diaries</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0901</span></div>\n<h2>A State Court Authorization Couldn&#x27;t Beat a County Sheriff&#x27;s &#x27;No Contract&#x27;</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A state court&#x27;s authorization doesn&#x27;t cover a county courthouse, turning a commissioned security test into burglary. Even after all charges are dropped, the arrest record stays forever—the justice system can pay damages but can&#x27;t restore a clean name.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">penetration testing</span><span class=\"tag\">physical security</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Residual Connections: The Most Underrated Simple Hack in Deep Learning History ResNet is the most cited paper of the 21st century, but its real contribution isn&#x27;t deepening networks—it&#x27;s the residual stream, a working memory that lets models store and edit information, fundamentally changing our understanding of neural networks. WelchLabsVideo WelchLabsVideo The most cited paper of the century is a brilliant hack Residual Networks Deep Learning Transformer Working Memory Vision Models Architecture Residual stream Skip connection Register tokens Shattered gradients problem\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-01-welchlabsvideo-残差连接-深度学习史上最被低估的简单-hack/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/a540a5f22c57ac52-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"W\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">WelchLabsVideo</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0901</span></div>\n<h2>Residual Connections: The Most Underrated Simple Hack in Deep Learning History</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">ResNet is the most cited paper of the 21st century, but its real contribution isn&#x27;t deepening networks—it&#x27;s the residual stream, a working memory that lets models store and edit information, fundamentally changing our understanding of neural networks.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Residual Networks</span><span class=\"tag\">Deep Learning</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Fed Credibility Shatters, Options Market Shrugs The Fed&#x27;s credibility broke over a single skipped hike, yet the options market prices Fed days like any other—cheap insurance may be an illusion. Excess Returns Excess Returns Sticky Inflation. Cheap Volatility. A Less Predictable Fed. Why Aren’t Markets More Worried? Fed Volatility Options Strategy Inflation Midterm Elections AI Writing forward volatility demand-based inflation zero DTE straddle jawboning financial repression calendarized gamma\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-excessreturns-美联储信誉崩塌-期权市场却当无事发生/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3cac5e72b6049e76-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:02:28</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Excess Returns</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Fed Credibility Shatters, Options Market Shrugs</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The Fed&#x27;s credibility broke over a single skipped hike, yet the options market prices Fed days like any other—cheap insurance may be an illusion.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Fed</span><span class=\"tag\">Volatility</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"China&#x27;s Economic Peak Has Passed: Credit Dries Up, Deflation Looms China&#x27;s share of global GDP peaked in 2021 and has been declining since; credit growth has fallen from 18% to 5%, and real growth may be only 1.5%-2%; the US has outperformed for five consecutive years. The narrative of industrial chain dominance is disproven by data; the future looks more like Japan-style deflation. Geopolitics Decanted with Dmitri Alperovitch Geopolitics Decanted with Dmitri Alperovitch The Miracle Is Over: Inside China&#x27;s Slow-Motion Economic Decay China economy credit PPP demographics US-China competition trade protection PPP / Purchasing Power Parity Impossible Trinity / Trilemma Loan Prime Rate (LPR) Special Revenue Bonds Total Factor Productivity (TFP) Demand-side Controls\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-geopoliticsdec-中国经济巅峰已过-美国优势还将扩大/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/8de827bd7254104a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"G\"><span class=\"dur\">47:58</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\">Geopolitics Decanted with Dmitri Alperovitch</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>China&#x27;s Economic Peak Has Passed: Credit Dries Up, Deflation Looms</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">China&#x27;s share of global GDP peaked in 2021 and has been declining since; credit growth has fallen from 18% to 5%, and real growth may be only 1.5%-2%; the US has outperformed for five consecutive years. The narrative of industrial chain dominance is disproven by data; the future looks more like Japan-style deflation.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">China economy</span><span class=\"tag\">credit</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Bell Used Einstein&#x27;s Own Tools to Refute His Core Argument The EPR argument forces a choice between an incomplete quantum description and action at a distance; determinism is never an assumption but a conclusion that is inferred. The full logic of Bell&#x27;s theorem must start here. Theories of Everything with Curt Jaimungal Theories of Everything with Curt Jaimungal Tim Maudlin: Quantum Nonlocality Explained FROM SCRATCH Quantum Mechanics EPR Bell&#x27;s Theorem Nonlocality History of Physics Action at a Distance EPR action at a distance configuration space reality criterion ontological locality dynamical locality\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-theoriesofever-贝尔用爱因斯坦自己的工具推翻了他的核心论点/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/06123fc0486c117a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">3:18:36</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Theories of Everything with Curt Jaimungal</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Bell Used Einstein&#x27;s Own Tools to Refute His Core Argument</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The EPR argument forces a choice between an incomplete quantum description and action at a distance; determinism is never an assumption but a conclusion that is inferred. The full logic of Bell&#x27;s theorem must start here.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Quantum Mechanics</span><span class=\"tag\">EPR</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"The Quantum Endgame Isn&#x27;t Cleaner Qubits — It&#x27;s Who Can Use a Phone-Chip Fab Line The quantum endgame isn&#x27;t about who has cleaner qubits — it&#x27;s about who can mass-produce using existing semiconductor fabs. Silicon spin qubits reuse TSMC lithography, while ion traps are stuck at a hundred thousand laser beams and superconductors at warehouse-sized refrigerators. From First Principles From First Principles Why Spin Qubits Will Win the Quantum Race (Part 2) (EP 55) Quantum Computing Silicon Spin Semiconductors Superconducting Ion Trap AI Auto-Tuning transmon valley splitting 2DEG DETR exchange-only qubit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-fromfirstprinc-硅自旋将赢-百万比特只需一块硅晶圆/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3248f02d6e6be9fe-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"F\"><span class=\"dur\">3:46:20</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">From First Principles</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>The Quantum Endgame Isn&#x27;t Cleaner Qubits — It&#x27;s Who Can Use a Phone-Chip Fab Line</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The quantum endgame isn&#x27;t about who has cleaner qubits — it&#x27;s about who can mass-produce using existing semiconductor fabs. Silicon spin qubits reuse TSMC lithography, while ion traps are stuck at a hundred thousand laser beams and superconductors at warehouse-sized refrigerators.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Quantum Computing</span><span class=\"tag\">Silicon Spin</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI Chip Shipments Will Jump an Order of Magnitude: From a Million to 15 Million Broadcom&#x27;s president shows an AI chip roadmap: from a million units to 15 million, with the &#x27;beast&#x27; being the largest package of 8 stackable compute dies plus 16 HBM modules, and four of the five frontier labs are collaborating. TechTechPotato TechTechPotato Future GPUs Will Look Like This custom chips ASIC advanced packaging HBM Broadcom compute supply chain back-end design services HBM CoWoS scaleup fabric\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-techtechpotato-未来-ai-定制芯片的形态-一只带-16-个-hbm-的巨兽/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/7f1cfd222dffd8f1-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">11:10</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">TechTechPotato</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>AI Chip Shipments Will Jump an Order of Magnitude: From a Million to 15 Million</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Broadcom&#x27;s president shows an AI chip roadmap: from a million units to 15 million, with the &#x27;beast&#x27; being the largest package of 8 stackable compute dies plus 16 HBM modules, and four of the five frontier labs are collaborating.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">custom chips</span><span class=\"tag\">ASIC</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"An Explorer Died for a Fictional City, and It All Started with a Political Forgery Percy Fawcett&#x27;s Amazon expeditions are often told as adventure legends, but the real starting point was border disputes fueled by the rubber trade; his narrative of &#x27;respect&#x27; for indigenous people is a gross oversimplification, and the City of Z that obsessed him may rest on a forged manuscript. Stuff You Missed in History Class Stuff You Missed in History Class Percy Fawcett, Manuscript 512, and a Lost City in the Amazon, Pt. 1 exploration history Amazon rubber trade indigenous peoples occultism lost city Manuscript 512 Royal Geographical Society rubber boom Mato Grosso City of Z\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-stuffmissed-福西特不是去冒险-是去给橡胶资本画地图/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/88586eb98e196b1a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">34:06</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Stuff You Missed in History Class</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>An Explorer Died for a Fictional City, and It All Started with a Political Forgery</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Percy Fawcett&#x27;s Amazon expeditions are often told as adventure legends, but the real starting point was border disputes fueled by the rubber trade; his narrative of &#x27;respect&#x27; for indigenous people is a gross oversimplification, and the City of Z that obsessed him may rest on a forged manuscript.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">exploration history</span><span class=\"tag\">Amazon</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Time Is Not an Illusion: Irreversibility Is More Fundamental Than Symmetric Equations Jim Al-Khalili argues that time is real and directed, and that irreversibility is more fundamental than time-symmetric equations; he also proposes using quantum entanglement entropy instead of thermodynamic entropy as the basis for the past hypothesis. Sean Carroll&#x27;s Mindscape Mindscape 366 | Jim Al-Khalili on Time, Quantum, Biology, and Cosmology arrow of time quantum mechanics quantum biology entropy past hypothesis philosophy of physics past hypothesis entanglement entropy master equation decoherence non-Markovian many-worlds interpretation\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-mindscape-时间的方向性比时间对称方程更根本/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/d69097efcbd03611-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">1:15:16</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Sean Carroll&#x27;s Mindscape</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Time Is Not an Illusion: Irreversibility Is More Fundamental Than Symmetric Equations</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Jim Al-Khalili argues that time is real and directed, and that irreversibility is more fundamental than time-symmetric equations; he also proposes using quantum entanglement entropy instead of thermodynamic entropy as the basis for the past hypothesis.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">arrow of time</span><span class=\"tag\">quantum mechanics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Most Gazans Have Abandoned Hamas, and the Window for Disarmament Is Opening Ahmed Fouad Alkhatib, a policy scholar born in Gaza, argues with four layers of opposition, two polls, and demographic data that most Gazans have long been anti-Hamas, and Hamas may be forced to disarm in stages; but host Russ&#x27;s pessimistic reminder: disarmament for Hamas equals political suicide. EconTalk EconTalk Hamas and the Future of Gaza (with Ahmed Fouad Alkhatib) Gaza Hamas Israeli-Palestinian conflict poll manipulation demilitarization Middle East geopolitics Shikaki polls NCAG Great Reset UNRWA DSA\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-econtalk-加沙多数人已抛弃哈马斯-缴械窗口正在打开/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/f8da698e33560635-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:22:48</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">EconTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Most Gazans Have Abandoned Hamas, and the Window for Disarmament Is Opening</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Ahmed Fouad Alkhatib, a policy scholar born in Gaza, argues with four layers of opposition, two polls, and demographic data that most Gazans have long been anti-Hamas, and Hamas may be forced to disarm in stages; but host Russ&#x27;s pessimistic reminder: disarmament for Hamas equals political suicide.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Gaza</span><span class=\"tag\">Hamas</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"US Economic Resilience Comes from Consumers Borrowing from the Future Barkin explains why consumption stays strong despite high prices: consumers cut savings, skip bills, and delay loan payments to keep spending; AI investment so far is more about price hikes and crowding out than productivity gains; the Fed may face a long headwind. Odd Lots Odd Lots Richmond Fed’s Tom Barkin on the Surprisingly Resilient Real Economy consumer resilience Federal Reserve AI capex inflation data centers tariffs SEP dot plot R-star forward guidance private label\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-oddlots-美国经济韧性来自消费者向未来借钱/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">31:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>US Economic Resilience Comes from Consumers Borrowing from the Future</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Barkin explains why consumption stays strong despite high prices: consumers cut savings, skip bills, and delay loan payments to keep spending; AI investment so far is more about price hikes and crowding out than productivity gains; the Fed may face a long headwind.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">consumer resilience</span><span class=\"tag\">Federal Reserve</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"America&#x27;s Treasury Secretary Threatens Allies with Divine Wrath, Proving He Has No Cards Treasury Secretary Bessent portrays the US as an angry god, demanding allies submit as if to Pascal&#x27;s wager. Farrell sees through the editorial: the louder the threat, the more it proves the US lacks the means to follow through, and allies are already hedging. Hidden Forces Hidden Forces Bessent&#x27;s Wager and Why the World is Calling America&#x27;s Bluff | Henry Farrell trade war dollar system geopolitics US institutions financial sanctions Pascal&#x27;s wager weaponized interdependence flexible realism unitary executive neo-royalism busted flush\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-hiddenforces-美国财长用神罚威胁盟国-反而证明手里没牌/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2b4203c8f6331570-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"H\"><span class=\"dur\">51:39</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Hidden Forces</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>America&#x27;s Treasury Secretary Threatens Allies with Divine Wrath, Proving He Has No Cards</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Treasury Secretary Bessent portrays the US as an angry god, demanding allies submit as if to Pascal&#x27;s wager. Farrell sees through the editorial: the louder the threat, the more it proves the US lacks the means to follow through, and allies are already hedging.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">trade war</span><span class=\"tag\">dollar system</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Consciousness Has No Finish Line: The Brain Is a Multiple Draft, Not a Theater Dennett rejects the &quot;Cartesian Theater&quot;: there is no single finish line where all sensations converge into consciousness; the brain is a set of parallel judgments that never get summed up into one show. Even &quot;when you became conscious&quot; often has no factual answer. The Partially Examined Life Partially Examined Life Ep. 399: Dan Dennett&#x27;s Model of Mind (Part One) consciousness philosophy mind model multiple drafts cognitive science Cartesian Theater Multiple Drafts Model Phi phenomenon Qualia Homunculus Stalinesque vs. Orwellian\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-pel-笛卡尔剧场不存在-意识不是放映-而是多重草稿/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/5a66360fe1170966-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">47:34</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Partially Examined Life</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Consciousness Has No Finish Line: The Brain Is a Multiple Draft, Not a Theater</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Dennett rejects the &quot;Cartesian Theater&quot;: there is no single finish line where all sensations converge into consciousness; the brain is a set of parallel judgments that never get summed up into one show. Even &quot;when you became conscious&quot; often has no factual answer.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">consciousness</span><span class=\"tag\">philosophy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"The Hard Part of Dementia Care Isn&#x27;t the Dementia Patient, It&#x27;s the Caregiver Who Gets Dragged Down The difficulty of dementia care lies not in the patient&#x27;s condition itself, but in the caregivers who are worn down day after day—care turns wives into nurses and forces post-90s to quit their jobs. Love is the starting point but not the support; the system has yet to catch up with these families. 不合时宜 不合时宜 漫长的告别：失智症、照护者与终将老去的我们 dementia elder care caregivers long-term care insurance aging only children Hogeweyk The Soul of Care informal care long-term care insurance wet-on-wet watercolor\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-cn300980-失智照护的难不在失智老人-而在会被拖垮的照护者/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/bda8c0f9bba83da6-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"不\"><span class=\"dur\">1:04:00</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">不合时宜</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>The Hard Part of Dementia Care Isn&#x27;t the Dementia Patient, It&#x27;s the Caregiver Who Gets Dragged Down</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The difficulty of dementia care lies not in the patient&#x27;s condition itself, but in the caregivers who are worn down day after day—care turns wives into nurses and forces post-90s to quit their jobs. Love is the starting point but not the support; the system has yet to catch up with these families.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">dementia</span><span class=\"tag\">elder care</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"The Bottleneck in a Fab Isn&#x27;t the Lithography Machine—It&#x27;s the OHT Robots on the Ceiling What really limits capacity in a wafer fab isn&#x27;t just the lithography machine, but the OHT vehicles shuttling overhead. The 300mm transition made them essential, and today the market is a duopoly of Daifuku and Muratec. Asianometry Asianometry The Little Ceiling Robots Inside a Semiconductor Fab AMHS OHT semiconductor manufacturing wafer fab automated logistics equipment duopoly AMHS / Automated Material Handling System FOUP / Front-Opening Unified Pod OHT / Overhead Hoist Transport Stocker Interbay / Intrabay\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-asianometry-别只盯着光刻机-天花板上的-oht-小车也在卡产能/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/c6301489e9b3f727-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">20:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>The Bottleneck in a Fab Isn&#x27;t the Lithography Machine—It&#x27;s the OHT Robots on the Ceiling</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">What really limits capacity in a wafer fab isn&#x27;t just the lithography machine, but the OHT vehicles shuttling overhead. The 300mm transition made them essential, and today the market is a duopoly of Daifuku and Muratec.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AMHS</span><span class=\"tag\">OHT</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The Treasury Secretary Trades the Bond Market Like a Position — and Prices Will Win US Treasury Secretary Bessent is intervening in the bond market, trade, and sanctions with a trader&#x27;s mindset, but inflation and deficits keep prices rising, making his strategy likely hollow. Patrick Boyle Patrick Boyle Scott Bessent Is at War With Prices — and Prices Are Winning! Treasury Fiscal Policy Inflation Federal Reserve Cryptocurrency Trade War TGA (Treasury General Account) On-the-run vs off-the-run bonds Duration neutral Term premium Stablecoin\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-patrickboyle-贝森特与价格的战争-财政部长的宏观赌局/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2eb71149af422d0e-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">44:51</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Patrick Boyle</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>The Treasury Secretary Trades the Bond Market Like a Position — and Prices Will Win</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">US Treasury Secretary Bessent is intervening in the bond market, trade, and sanctions with a trader&#x27;s mindset, but inflation and deficits keep prices rising, making his strategy likely hollow.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Treasury</span><span class=\"tag\">Fiscal Policy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Elite Universities Are a Cartel: Selling Status, Not Education America&#x27;s elite universities are not charitable educational institutions but a cartel that maintains its brand by freezing enrollment, cultivating alumni donations, and securing federal research grants; they sell status, not education. Modern MBA Modern MBA The American College Cartel University Finance Endowments Elite Education Admissions Insider American Innovation endowment advancement provost tenure yield tech tree\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-modernmba-精英大学是制造稀缺的卡特尔-而非教育机构/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3676f3a101faa05c-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"M\"><span class=\"dur\">45:11</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Modern MBA</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Elite Universities Are a Cartel: Selling Status, Not Education</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">America&#x27;s elite universities are not charitable educational institutions but a cartel that maintains its brand by freezing enrollment, cultivating alumni donations, and securing federal research grants; they sell status, not education.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">University Finance</span><span class=\"tag\">Endowments</span>\n</div></div></a>"]